    {
      "box": [
        90.0,
        190.47470092773438,
        518.695068359375,
        348.3536071777344
      ],
      "text": "23.It is essential to adopt strategies which involve and help residents of the\nregion.\n24.Interventions which reduce heat are absolutely vital for our survival in\nthis location.\n25.More work will need to be done in future decades to deal with the\nimpact of rising water levels.\n26.The number of locations requiring action to adapt to flooding has grown\nin recent years.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        361.29205322265625,
        150.1049041748047,
        380.79345703125
      ],
      "text": "List of People\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        75.12000274658203,
        381.2746887207031,
        188.74774169921875,
        479.51361083984375
      ],
      "text": "A. Yanira Pineda\nB. Susanna Tol\nC. Elizabeth English\nD. Raisa Chowdhury\nE. Greg Spotts\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        494.4920349121094,
        276.3106689453125,
        513.9934692382812
      ],
      "text": "A new role for livestock guard dogs\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        528.6347045898438,
        526.8172607421875,
        566.7137451171875
      ],
      "text": "Livestock guard dogs, traditionally used to protect farm animals from predators,\nare now being used to protect the predators themselves\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        580.1710205078125,
        84.2708969116211,
        599.6724243164062
      ],
      "text": "A.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        600.1536865234375,
        518.4581909179688,
        738.2335815429688
      ],
      "text": "For thousands of years, livestock guard dogs worked alongside shepherds to\nprotect their sheep, goats and cattle from predators such as wolves and bears.\nBut in the 19th and 20th centuries, when such predators were largely\nexterminated, most guard dogs lost their jobs. In recent years, however, as\nincreased efforts have been made to protect wild animals, predators have\nbecome more widespread again. As a result, farmers once more need to\nprotect their livestock, and guard dogs are enjoying an unexpected revival.\n"
    }
  ]
